<urn:atm:triage:finding/WINRACE-001-AL16MVP>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "WINRACE-001-AL16MVP" ;
  triage:title "axum_route_hook_timeout_returns_success_warning_and_cancels_hook_future fails on Windows CI, reproducibly" ;
  triage:description "PR #814 (feature/al16-hermes-atm-mvp, base integrate/phase-al) has failed Test (windows-latest) twice in a row on the same test: crates/atm-http-runtime/src/storage_and_nudge_router.rs:1915, axum_route_hook_timeout_returns_success_warning_and_cancels_hook_future, panicking with 'timed-out hook is advisory after the durable write'. quality-mgr confirmed recurrence (not a one-off flake) and identified this as Windows-only timing-sensitive code in atm-http-runtime (the Tokio+Axum target runtime, not legacy daemon) -- in scope for direct fix, not a remodel of frozen legacy code. arch-ctm independently flagged this same failure as unrelated to the AL16/AL19 Hermes-release blocker (BLOCKER-AL16-HERMES-RELEASE-001) and asked that it be triaged/fixed as its own atm-http-runtime finding, not routed through hermes-atm. PR #814 remains gated on the Hermes blocker regardless of this fix's outcome." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-al" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "flaky-test" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
